<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Operation Car Wash</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2014">2014</a>–<a href="/years/2021">2021</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a> · Also known as Lava Jato, Operação Lava Jato</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Operation Car Wash, or Lava Jato, was a Brazilian criminal investigation launched in 2014 that uncovered a vast system of bribes paid by construction firms to executives of the state oil company <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrobras">Petrobras</a> and to politicians. It led to the conviction of many businessmen and politicians, including former president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luiz-inacio-lula-da-silva">Lula</a>, whose convictions were later annulled. The scandal deepened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>'s political crisis around the impeachment of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dilma-rousseff">Dilma Rousseff</a>, and the task force was wound up in 2021.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/operation-car-wash.jpg" alt="Operation Car Wash" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bageense · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Montagem_Lava_Jato.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Background</h2><p>The first accusation came in 2008 from the businessman Hermes Magnus, who reported an attempt to launder money through his electronics firm, Dunel Indústria e Comércio. The inquiry that opened in March 2014 began with a small car wash in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brasilia">Brasília</a> and identified four criminal rings of black-market currency dealers, headed by Carlos Habib Chater, Alberto Youssef, Nelma Kodama and Raul Henrique Srour. Federal prosecutors led by Deltan Dallagnol gathered the evidence, and Judge Sergio Moro was in charge of the operation.</p><p>The case widened when investigators found that Youssef had bought a Range Rover Evoque for Paulo Roberto Costa, a former director of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrobras">Petrobras</a>. Once charged, Costa agreed to cooperate under a new law of rewarded collaboration, a form of plea bargaining, and his testimony showed which political parties controlled the company.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Course of events</h2><p>According to investigators, political appointees in state enterprises extorted bribes from suppliers, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrobras">Petrobras</a> directors took kickbacks of 1% to 5% of payments. Part of the money funded the campaigns of parties such as the MDB, PT, PSDB and PP. A cartel of engineering firms, among them Odebrecht, Grupo OAS and Andrade Gutierrez, was said to share contracts, including stadiums for the 2014 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fifa-world-cup">FIFA World Cup</a> and the Belo Monte Dam. In April 2015 Petrobras reported $2.1 billion in bribes.</p><p>On 8 March 2016 Marcelo Odebrecht was sentenced to 19 years in prison. In April 2018 former president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luiz-inacio-lula-da-silva">Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva</a> entered prison in Curitiba. Prosecutors cooperated with authorities in 61 countries, and the Odebrecht inquiries reached presidents and candidates in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Aftermath and significance</h2><p>In January 2019 Moro left the bench to become justice minister under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jair-bolsonaro">Jair Bolsonaro</a>, Lula's leading rival in the 2018 election, a move that drew criticism. From 9 June 2019 The Intercept Brasil published Telegram messages, hacked by Walter Delgatti Neto, that were said to show improper coordination between Moro and the prosecutors; Moro and Dallagnol denied wrongdoing. The leaks turned public opinion against the probe, Lula was released on 8 November 2019 after a Supreme Federal Court ruling, and the task force was disbanded on 1 February 2021. Companies and individuals agreed to pay 25 billion reais in fines and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/repatriation-of-cultural-property">restitution</a>.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Operation Car Wash” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>His successor Dilma Rousseff was impeached in 2016 amid recession and the <b>Car Wash</b> corruption investigation.</blockquote><a href="/state/new-republic-brazil">New Republic (Brazil)</a></li></ul></section>
